# GitHub does not know Beans, and `.b` is claimed by three languages it does
# know — B, Brainfuck and Limbo — so Linguist classifies each file by guess and
# splits one codebase across all three. `linguist-language=Beans` cannot fix
# that: an override is only honoured for a language already in Linguist's list,
# and the bar for adding one is 2000+ files indexed across many unrelated public
# repositories.
#
# So highlight as Swift, the closest language GitHub does know — it shares
# class, let, var, init, override, import, enum, struct, self, super and
# @annotations — and keep the guesses out of the repository language bar
# altogether, rather than trade one wrong answer for another.
*.b  linguist-language=Swift linguist-detectable=false
*.bx linguist-language=Swift linguist-detectable=false
